quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  34,23,"No intercession will be of any benefit in His presence except by those to whom He has (already) granted permission. When fear is banished from their hearts, they will ask: ‘What has your Lord said?’ They will say: ‘The truth. And He is the All-Exalted, the All-Great.’"
  34,24,"Say: ‘Who provides you sustenance from the heavens and the earth?’ Say: ‘Allah (is the One Who provides). Indeed, (either) we or you (i.e. one of us) must be upon guidance or in manifest error.’"
  34,25,"Say: ‘You will not be questioned about what we were guilty of, nor shall we be questioned about what you do.’"
  34,26,"Say: ‘Our Lord will bring us together, then He will judge between us with justice. And He is the Greatest Judge, the All-Knowing.’"
  34,27,"Say: ‘Show me those whom you associate with Him as partners. No, indeed! (They can never show any such partner). Instead, He (alone) is Allah, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.’"
  34,28,"We have not sent you except as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner to all of humankind, but most people do not know."
  34,29,And they say: ‘When will this promise (of the Last Day) be fulfilled if you are truthful?’
  34,30,Say: ‘You (already) have the appointment of a day that you will neither delay nor advance by a single moment.’
  34,31,"The disbelievers say: ‘We will never believe in this Qur’an, nor in what was (revealed) before it.’ If only you could see when the wrongdoers would be made to stand before their Lord, throwing blame at each other. Those who had been oppressed will say to those who were arrogant: ‘Had it not been for you, we would surely have been believers.’"
